dArkOS RG52 Mini - NPU UPSCALE: third-party components
=======================================================

NPU UPSCALE enlarges an emulator's native frame with a small neural network on the RK3562's
NPU, inside dArkOS's Vulkan rotate layer (VK_LAYER_DARKOS_rotate). It uses:

1. librknnrt.so - Rockchip RKNN runtime 2.5.0
   Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
   Under the License Agreement for RKNN Software Development Kit Package (its full text is
   /usr/share/doc/librknnrt/LICENSE, npusr/LICENSE.rknn in the dArkOS sources, from the same
   release): for applications compatible with Rockchip's products (1.1), its notices kept
   (2.1(b)). dArkOS uses it only on the RK3562 of the RG52 Mini. Unmodified, as
   published in https://github.com/airockchip/rknn-toolkit2 at the tag v2.5.0,
   rknpu2/runtime/Linux/librknn_api/aarch64/librknnrt.so
   sha256 4b6cc575bedf8952b13db4b1190fa3b3d2ac213f00be774ff6ccd19d651970c0
   Installed as /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/librknnrt.so; loaded by the layer only when a game
   starts with NPU UPSCALE on.

2. rknn_api.h - the runtime's header, from the same release and under the same license
   (vk-rotate-layer/rknn_api.h in the dArkOS sources; LICENSE.rknn beside it).

3. The 3DS's model, /usr/share/darkos/npusr/espcn_x3_400x240.rknn: ESPCN x3
   From TF-ESPCN by Fanny Monori, https://github.com/fannymonori/TF-ESPCN (the models OpenCV's
   dnn_superres module uses), Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-TF-ESPCN, installed beside this file).
   Changed: the first layer rebuilt for the NPU (the same network, its 5x5 kernel as five rows),
   quantised to INT8 with rknn-toolkit2 2.5.0 for x3 from 400x240; npusr/models/make_espcn.py
   in the dArkOS sources makes it from ESPCN_x3.pb (TF-ESPCN's export/ file, kept there too).
   sha256 aa9ccd9cc62555c40d178db133ab3a8d8269714093dd86a9cbf5ee922b559e68  espcn_x3_400x240.rknn

4. The PSP's model, /usr/share/darkos/npusr/espcn_x2_480x272.rknn (the file name the layer
   looks for; the network is not ESPCN): made for dArkOS in 2026, x2 from 480x272.
   A space-to-depth network (4 luma channels of a 2x2 cell in, 7 3x3 convolutions, 52 048
   weights), 2.4 times faster than ESPCN x2 on the NPU. Its weights started from a bicubic
   interpolation written into the network plus random noise (seed 0) - no other network's
   weights - and were trained to give what ESPCN x2 (item 3's TF-ESPCN, ESPCN_x2.pb, Apache
   License 2.0) gives on the same inputs: screenshots of PSP and 3DS games taken on the console;
   scikit-image's sample photographs (skimage.data: astronaut, coffee, chelsea, rocket, camera,
   coins, moon, page, text - public domain or CC0 by their notes there; moon and page have no
   note of their own and come with scikit-image under its BSD-3-Clause license); shapes, text
   and textures the training script draws. No image dataset. Quantised to INT8 with
   rknn-toolkit2 2.5.0, calibrated on 20 PSP screenshots.
   In the dArkOS sources: npusr/models/s2d_distill.py trains it, s2d_rknn.py makes the .rknn
   from its weights (s2d_x2_v7.pt, kept there: training on a GPU is not bit-exact). The
   screenshots are not in the sources.
   sha256 d2cf6854545702c7331b3747527170047894feba658a6bf1c06a49488fa88bbc  espcn_x2_480x272.rknn
